commit 026d4401322be01c449ccf29bf04ad6842b56ba6
Author: marcin p. joachimiak <4625870+realmarcin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 18 15:12:06 2026 -0700

    Salt dedup (batch 5): merge 7 garbled typo-duplicates; enrich 2 deferred
    
    Resolves the "no-source-confirmation" garbled salts from NEXT_TASKS item 3 using
    Edison deep research + MediaDive recipe context + a PK-collision check. Recipe
    context (each appears among trace metals; the correctly-spelled salt appears in
    sibling recipes) plus the existing mapped records showed these 0-occurrence
    orphans are typo-duplicates of compounds ALREADY mapped in MIM — so they were
    merged (absorbed as RAW_TEXT synonyms + MERGED_FROM_UNMAPPED_DUPLICATE history),
    not freshly mapped. A merge asserts no new SSSOM row, which honors Edison's
    "don't exactMatch a malformed label" caution.
    
    Merged (7):
    - Na2Mo4 / Na2MoO7 / Na2MoO7O4 x 2 H2O -> Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O (CHEBI:75213)
    - Na2WO2 x 2 H2O -> Na2WO4 x 2 H2O (CHEBI:63939)
    - Na2Se2O3 -> Na2SeO3 (CHEBI:48843)
    - Na2S2SO3 -> Na2S2O3 (CHEBI:132112)
    - MnCl4 x 4 H2O -> MnCl2 x 4 H2O (CHEBI:86368)
    
    Enriched in place, left UNMAPPED (Edison findings + reason):
    - Fe(SO4)3 x n H2O -> iron(III) sulfate hydrate (candidate CHEBI:131387, closeMatch);
      malformed + unspecified hydrate, Fe sulfate hydrates are distinct CAS substances.
    - MnCl4 x 6 H2O -> manganese(II) chloride; non-standard hexahydrate, no CHEBI term.
    
    unmapped 390 -> 383. Gates green: reconcile GAP/ORPHAN/STALE 0, SSSOM invariants
    A/B1/B2/B3, validate-products (id<->label ✅), validate-strict 0 ERROR rows.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

